have an answer for that one? I really don't know the answer to that. I'm curious if Dr. de Blume does because I haven't seen a study that asked that question. I mean, you know, I can imagine, obviously, if you're a working adult, you know, the stress is going to start increasing the longer that you're away. And, you know, we know that for some people, when they get back to work, it can be worse. You know, like if the stress and you haven't kept up with things and, you know, there's a million emails in your inbox that you have to deal with and that there's things that you were supposed to do that you didn't do. That's obviously going to create, you know, it's going to potentially wash out the benefits of the vacation when you get back.

