22
00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:44.000
you also can really wonder what kind of people do you attract for these studies. So it would never render very good results, I think. So that makes it very hard to investigate the duration. But overall, we do not see this dose response relationship that you would maybe expect that the longer the holiday, the longer lasting the effects are. So what I think more and more when I look at research on vacations, but also on shorter respites from work, think of breaks, lunch breaks and so on, that I think the regularity and having a regular breakout times, that's maybe much more important than having a long time out.

